# Secrets
# .env is built by svc-build-env.sh from the box's pragma file and is
# never committed. .env.example is tracked; it holds no secrets, only
# the declaration of what needs filling. There are no .env.live /
# .env.staging overlays — a box runs ONE instance, so .env is the only
# env layer and this is the only pattern that may be ignored. A blanket
# .env* would also swallow .env.example, and the stack would then start
# on defaults in every fresh clone.
.env

# Temp/cleanup scripts
ghcr-purge.sh

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Nothing here ignores service data. postgres and redis write to
# ${HOST_DATA_ROOT} (/srv/data/<appname> by default), which is
# outside the repo on purpose — a data directory under a git working
# tree is one `git clean` away from gone.

# public/nginx/html is NOT ignored. The built frontend is committed
# there, because commit -> push -> pull is the only way files reach a
# server and a standalone deploy has to be able to serve it. There is
# ONE bundle directory, html/saamsaam — a box runs one instance, so
# there is no second html/saamsaam-staging to keep in step. The build
# lands here first, then gets copied into the shared provider's
# nginx/html (local-infra on the dev box, gentick-infra on a server)
# on hosts where that stack is the one serving.
